            "question_id": 16221,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 927,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Overview",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"LhvxdlwoRowrFWxCj4llb7Acgje\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-XBJfdBH7joZ10qxt7t8l1SoVgZT\">Overall, Internet usage increased across all age groups throughout the given period. Notably, the youngest demographic (16-24 years) consistently maintained the highest rates of Internet use, while the eldest group (65 and over) recorded significantly lower percentages throughout the period.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 16221,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 928,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"LhvxdlwoRowrFWxCj4llb7Acgje\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Il4xdAwIIoh8D7xkdyflYN6ngxb\">Examining the three younger age brackets first, in 2003, approximately 80% of individuals aged 16-24 were Internet users, which was higher than both the 25-44 and 45-54 age groups, at around 50% and 60% respectively. The youngest cohort saw their figures rise to nearly 100% in 2005, though this decreased slightly to about 90% by 2006. In contrast, both the 25-44 and 45-54 age brackets exhibited steady upward trends, with both groups reaching approximately 80% usage by the end of the period.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 16221,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 929,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"LhvxdlwoRowrFWxCj4llb7Acgje\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-I2LRdsgEHox9Spxg8qrlb8vcgfx\">With respect to the older demographics, Internet usage among the 55-64 group stood at approximately 30% in 2003, while the eldest group (65+) had zero internet usage. The 55-64 bracket subsequently experienced significant growth to around 50% by the end of the period, whereas Internet usage among seniors remained relatively low, reaching just 20% in 2006.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 16221,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          }
